it's cpr awareness week and the red  cross is recognizing two officers for  their quick action they took to save a  life mary jane bellissa has our story  [Music]  it was quick thinking on trooper  christopher french and officer mike  smith's part that helped save a man's  life back in january 2020. trooper  french with the nevada highway patrol  responded to a reckless driving call  when he arrived he found a car stopped  in the middle of i-15 near flamingo the  driver was unconscious and not breathing  trooper french blocked traffic with his  car and immediately began performing cpr  there's no time to really think  how are we going to react to the  situation we do what we're trained to do  less than 10 minutes later officer smith  arrived to assist him with cpr once the  ambulance arrived they even followed the  man to the hospital we hope that the  outcome in the end is the best  and it was in this in this circumstance  i followed him to the hospital contacted  his family  waited there for the family to get there  made sure everything was set and he  understood everything that went on  before i even left i am so happy it made  me want to cry actually i found out that  he lived i'm like this guy  i thought for sure he was dead  once we put him on the ambulance i  thought he was dead but find out he was  alive forget about it that's awesome the  pair are now being hailed as heroes on  saturday the red cross presented their  life saving award for their efforts as  being trained to use cpr can make all  the difference between life and death  situations i really appreciate it i  still believe in the community the  community believes in law enforcement  and  having those personal partnerships with  the community as well as private  industry and other agencies is wonderful  and it feels really good to be  recognized mary jane balleza live local  now  cpr and first aid training classes are  also available at the red cross
 

